WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.094 --> 00:00:03.721
- [Narrator] This is wicket, a red panda.

00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:06.142
At 10 years old, Wicket
is a fully grown male

00:00:06.142 --> 00:00:08.343
with a height of just over two feet

00:00:08.343 --> 00:00:11.412
or slightly larger than
your average house cat.

00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:14.732
As cute as he is, his population
has decreased dramatically,

00:00:14.732 --> 00:00:17.162
with less than 10,000 left in the wild.

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:19.745
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.991 --> 00:00:24.250
Red panda in name, it
is not closely related

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.380
to the giant panda, but actually closer

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.990
to the raccoon family.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.310
He loves to eat bamboo,

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.180
but won't turn down the occasional bird,

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.597
insect or mammal for a snack.

00:00:35.642 --> 00:00:38.482
Native to the eastern Himalayas
and southwestern China,

00:00:38.482 --> 00:00:42.740
red pandas live in trees and
are nimble, agile climbers.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.280
Their reddish brown fur and
bushy tails camouflage them

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.180
in their habitat from
predators, like snow leopards.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.830
Besides other animals,
humans pose a major threat,

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.540
poaching and hunting them for their fur.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.660
The forests that they live
in are shrinking fast,

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.439
and estimates say that their
population has been cut in half

00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:01.189
in the last 20 years.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.683
This is the red panda.

